1 NOTE [Added by Claude research, 3 Sep 2026 - round 2] RESOLVED. Son of David Sisson and Mary Ragsdale of Gilmer Co. (the 1850 Gilmer &apos;Richard Sisson&apos; with wife Rosanna is his BROTHER Richard, who married Roseanna Deel, Elizabeth&apos;s sister)
2 CONC . 1860 census, Wilkes Co., GA, household 79/79: Larkin R. Scisson 45 farmer b. NC; Elizabeth 34 b. NC; William D. 17, Sarah E. 15, Thomas A. 13, Enoch C. 10, John G. 8, Martha S. 5, James J. 2, Eliza 2/12 (= Lou), all b. GA. Served in the Confedera
2 CONC te army under H. P. Arnold of Oglethorpe County; killed 28 Aug 1862, first day of Second Manassas. 1870 census, Wilkes Co. dist. 169, household 197/198: Elizabeth Sisson 43 keeping house; Thomas A. 22, Enoch C. 19, John G. 17, Martha S. 15, James J
2 CONC . 12, Louisa 10, Laura 8. Ten children now attached. Next: his compiled service record (likely 9th or 15th Georgia Infantry, both raised partly in Wilkes/Oglethorpe and both at Second Manassas) and a widow&apos;s pension application by Elizabeth i
2 CONC n Georgia Confederate Pension files.
