1 NOTE [Added by Claude research, 3 Sep 2026] DATE FIX: the original entry had birth &apos;About 1920&apos;, impossible for the father of Emma Ann D. Thaxton (b. 1861). Changed to an estimate of c.1830; no record found yet. Next step: 1870 Taliaferro Coun
2 CONC ty census (Emma age ~9 should be in a Thaxton household), and Taliaferro/Wilkes marriage records for a Thaxton-Arnold marriage c.1855-60. Note a later Thaxton-Lunceford marriage (Artie Bill Thaxton m. Vester Lunceford 1901) shows the families staye
2 CONC d connected.
2 CONT 
2 CONT [Added by Claude research, 3 Sep 2026 - round 2] LEAD: a &apos;Thaxton Cemetery&apos; is mapped about 4.6 miles from the Turner Family Cemetery on Philomath Road near Rayle, Wilkes County - i.e. in the Philomath/Rayle neighbourhood where the Comb
2 CONC s and Lunceford families lived. It is listed on BillionGraves with no headstones photographed yet. Peter Thaxton and Martha Arnold are very likely buried there; a photo request on BillionGraves/Find a Grave, or a visit, could yield their dates.
