2 PAGE Biography of Uriah Allen Rogers
1 SOUR @S1128836435@
2 PAGE 278W-5M3
1 NOTE [Added by Claude research, 3 Sep 2026] Said to have been born in North Carolina; parents undocumented (claims include Josiah Hill &amp; Frances Rogers, or Joseph &amp; Mary Ransom Rogers - neither proven). Moved to Georgia and married Asha Everett
2 CONC , daughter of planter John Everett. Settled on a small farm at the forks of the Canoochee River and Lott&apos;s Creek, just north of present-day Daisy, GA (then Bulloch, now Evans County), across the creek from the Everett plantation. Family story
2 CONC : went to Florida in 1830 and never returned, presumed killed by Indians. Years later sons Uriah and Ervin heard of a Thomas Rogers who died leaving unclaimed property near present-day downtown Dallas, Texas; Uriah rode to Texas but was not convinc
2 CONC ed it was his father. Five known children: Uriah Allen (1808-1882), Nancy (1810-1893), William (b. 5 Sep 1814), Ervin Green (1818-1899), John (b. 19 May 1820); William and John are not named in John Everett&apos;s 1840 will and may have died young
2 CONC . FamilySearch gives his name as Thomas Stephen Rogers.
