1 NOTE [Added by Claude research, 3 Sep 2026] Daughter of planter John Everett (1747-1841) of Lott&apos;s Creek, Bulloch County. After her husband Thomas Rogers disappeared c.1830 she moved her family back to be near her father. Surname also spelled Everi
2 CONC tt.
2 CONT 
2 CONT [Added by Claude research, 3 Sep 2026 - round 2] FATHER QUESTION: the Mulligan biography says Asha was the daughter of &apos;John Everett (1747-1841)&apos;. WikiTree (Everett-981) documents a John Everett b. 1754 Tyrrell Co., NC, d. 1820, Revolutio
2 CONC nary veteran of the NC militia (wounded at Bettis&apos; Bridge, 4 Aug 1781, carrying the rifle ball for life), who married Sarah Fagan in 1772 and moved to Bulloch County in 1785 with six children (a seventh born in GA 1789); he served as county co
2 CONC mmissioner, JP, militia officer and state representative, owning 1,460 acres in Bulloch and 800 in Effingham; daughter Hannah married Charles McCall Sr. The Everett Family Bible record (NC Archives) says there were THREE John Everetts plus a Jehu
2 CONC . Asha (b. 1786) fits as a Georgia-born child of John &amp; Sarah Fagan Everett OR as a child of the older John (1747-1841). The Bulloch marriage index has &apos;EVERITT, John m. JONES, Mary 18 Mar 1807&apos; and &apos;EVERETT, John m. ELLIS, Eliza
2 CONC beth 22 Feb 1824&apos; - the 1807 marriage could be the elder John remarrying. Resolve with the 1840 will and the Bible record.
