1 NOTE [Added by Claude research, 3 Sep 2026 - round 2] Son of William Sisson (Revolutionary soldier) and Frances Shearin. Married Mary Ragsdale 1 Feb 1812, Rutherford Co., NC. Per &apos;Gilmer Co. Heritage&apos; (1996) David and Mary moved from Rutherfor
2 CONC d Co. to Buncombe Co., NC, then Habersham Co., GA, then Gilmer Co. (May 1847), settling in the Boardtown section, buying the Oz Miller farm on Boardtown Road and donating land for Buckhorn Baptist Church (now Mt. Pleasant Baptist). Drew in the 183
2 CONC 8 Georgia Cherokee Land Lottery; 1850 Gilmer census farmer, farm valued $1000; age 82 in 1870 Ellijay. Said to have owned 600 acres; also adopted two boys, Jack Dodd and George Holloway. Some researchers make him a son of William&apos;s brother Dav
2 CONC id rather than of William.
