1 NOTE [Added by Claude research, 3 Sep 2026 - round 2] Revolutionary War: 2nd Lieutenant in Capt. Butler&apos;s company of volunteers, 1 Sep 1781-1 Mar 1782 (DAR Magazine, Jan 1945); Lawrence Stanley (1977) says he served as a musician in a band in the R
2 CONC evolutionary army and, by tradition, was a fine fiddler who asked for his fiddle on his deathbed and played a last tune. NC land grant: 400 acres on both sides of the Pacolet River including Skull Shoal, Tryon Co. (surveyed 1766, granted 5 May 1769
2 CONC ). 12 Mar 1788 deeded one acre to the elders of the church on the Pacolet River near Skull Shoal for the meeting house. 1790 census Union Co., SC. Will names son Joshua executor. CAUTION: researcher Robert Hays Williams doubts the William born 173
2 CONC 9 to Thomas &amp; Hannah is the same man who died in SC in 1796 (a William Sisson sold land in NC in 1756). Wife Frances Shearin. Children: Joshua (c.1765-1830), Charles Bruce (1769-1832, Habersham Co. will 1832), Turner, William (c.1777), Thomas (
2 CONC c.1785), David (1789).
